# Privana Core Engineering Laws & Agent Invariants (.cursorrules)

1. Think Before Writing (Mandatory Pre-Flight Analysis):
   - ALWAYS produce an Architectural Dry-Run before generating code on complex tasks.
   - Trace data memory lifecycles and edge cases (NaN, null, empty datasets, zero variance).

2. Conciseness & Elegance Principle (The "10 vs 20 Line" Rule):
   - Choose idiomatic, high-leverage TypeScript/Arrow/DuckDB primitives.
   - Zero boilerplate bloat: avoid redundant wrappers or speculative abstractions.

3. Absolute Zero-Hardcoding Mandate:
   - ZERO hardcoded table names, column names (e.g. `gender`, `sleep_hours`), row counts, categorical labels, or schemas.
   - All columns, buckets, and metrics must be 100% dynamically inferred from dataset profiles.

4. Strict Layer Isolation:
   - DuckDB-WASM is strictly data access infrastructure in `src/domain/compute/duckdb/`.
   - Executors, NLU, and UI must NEVER import `@duckdb/duckdb-wasm` directly.
   - Arrow Materialization Boundary: Never convert full Arrow tables into JS arrays. Only compact aggregated records (~20-100 objects) cross into the UI thread.

5. Defensive Non-Breaking Migration:
   - All new engine work must be shadow-verified against `InMemoryComputeEngine`.
   - Existing tests must remain green at all times.
   - Feature-flag engine routing (`useDuckDB = false` default until verified).
